    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Beginning with version 2.5, Spring also provides support for a JCA-based "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MessageListener"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " container. The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "JmsMessageEndpointManager"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " tries to automatically determine the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ActivationSpec"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " class name from the provider’s "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ResourceAdapter"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " class name. Therefore, it is typically possible to provide Spring’s generic "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "JmsActivationSpecConfig"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./JmsConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Alternatively, you can set up a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "JmsMessageEndpointManager"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " with a given "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ActivationSpec"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " object. The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ActivationSpec"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " object may also come from a JNDI lookup (using "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<jee:jndi-lookup>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "). The following example shows how to do so:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "include-code::./AlternativeJmsConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "See the javadoc for "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsMessageEndpointManager"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/jms/listener/endpoint/JmsMessageEndpointManager.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JmsActivationSpecConfig"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/jms/listener/endpoint/JmsActivationSpecConfig.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", and "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ResourceAdapterFactoryBean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/jca/support/ResourceAdapterFactoryBean.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for more details."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Spring also provides a generic JCA message endpoint manager that is not tied to JMS: "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "org.springframework.jca.endpoint.GenericMessageEndpointManager"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". This component allows for using any message listener type (such as a JMS "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MessageListener"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ") and any provider-specific "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ActivationSpec"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " object. See your JCA provider’s documentation to find out about the actual capabilities of your connector, and see the "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "GenericMessageEndpointManager"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/jca/endpoint/GenericMessageEndpointManager.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " javadoc for the Spring-specific configuration details."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "JCA-based message endpoint management is very analogous to EJB 2.1 Message-Driven Beans. It uses the same underlying resource provider contract. As with EJB 2.1 MDBs, you can use any message listener interface supported by your JCA provider in the Spring context as well. Spring nevertheless provides explicit “convenience” support for JMS, because JMS is the most common endpoint API used with the JCA endpoint management contract."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Support for JCA Message Endpoints"
      }
    ]
  }
}
